; Frame lists of the room items: 34 frames of 4 bytes
;
; Each frame: +0 word: graphics address of a 16 x 16 pixel sprite (32 bytes, in the sprite block at #R$66DC), +2 byte:
; attribute, +3 byte: 0 (unused: it is popped as the flags of the sprite command). The type records (#R$8AA7) point
; into this table; the item's current frame number (slot +$0A) is an index in its list, read by #R$A7DB
; (DrawItemFrame). The lists:
; .
; FramesHeart (2 frames), FramesCross (12: 6 bright crosses in the colours of #R$8553, then 6 thin ones, the plus sign
; sprite), FramesCheckpoint (2: not active, active), FramesArch (9, all the arch with changing ink), FramesScroll
; (1: the parchment), FramesRedScroll (1: the same sprite in red, attribute $42), FramesBell (2: at rest, ringing),
; FramesLever (2: up, pulled), FramesWheel (2) and FramesChalice (1).
@label=FramesHeart
b$8B07 DEFW $682C
 $8B09 DEFB $02,$00
 $8B0B DEFW $684C
 $8B0D DEFB $02,$00
